{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VZWHSRCcNgwoFpUBTteiPJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Draft reference gap memo\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** ready (3 targets). No retrieval was run in this stage.\n4\t\n5\t## Summary\n6\tRelated work cites many peripheral conformal papers (class-conditional, efficiency, time series, clinical applications). It does not cite the foundational and directly-used sources: the baseline score functions, split/Mondrian conformal, and weighted conformal under covariate shift. `references.bib` contains no Vovk, Romano, Angelopoulos, Tibshirani (weighted) or Aitchison entries. The appendix already acknowledges that these are \"stated as background without citation\".\n7\t\n8\t## Missing literatures\n9\t- Split (inductive) and Mondrian conformal prediction foundations\n10\t- Weighted conformal prediction under covariate shift\n11\t- Conformal classification scores (LAC, APS, RAPS)\n12\t- Compositional data analysis (Aitchison log-ratio geometry)\n13\t\n14\t## Targets\n15\t\n16\t1. **baseline-score-sources** (high, comparator) — Method, \"Baselines, negative controls and validity conditions\". The headline claim is a margin over the best of LAC/APS/RAPS/class-wise LAC, yet none of these is cited. Search: LAC / least-ambiguous set classifiers; APS; RAPS; class-wise split conformal.\n17\t2. **mondrian-split-conformal-foundations** (high, background) — Method, \"Statistical background\". The Proposition and rank argument are called textbook but unsourced, and Mondrian calibration is the core of the method. Search: Mondrian conformal prediction (Vovk et al.); split/inductive conformal; distribution-free finite-sample coverage.\n18\t3. **weighted-conformal-shift-and-compositional-framing** (medium, positioning) — Method, \"Weighted calibration under covariate shift\", and Related Work, \"Positioning\". The gated weighting step and the shift axis lack their source (weighted conformal under covariate shift; classifier-based density ratios). The log-ratio compositional framing is uncited. Search: conformal under covariate shift; probabilistic-classifier density-ratio estimation; Aitchison compositional data.\n19\t\n20\t## Deliberately ignored\n21\t- Quantitative results (grounded in `paper_data.json`).\n22\t- Further applied or tutorial conformal papers, and the existing Related Work paragraphs on other output types.\n23\t- Real-data or CIFAR-10 literature, which would require reshaping the paper's synthetic-only scope.\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9c6cd30-b13b-4fc9-872d-c09885072b37","uuid":"002cdd84-fa52-478d-90dc-8b41c3514e0a","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:02:54.139Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/paper/draft_reference_gaps.md","content":"# Draft reference gap memo\n\n**Status:** ready (3 targets). No retrieval was run in this stage.\n\n## Summary\nRelated work cites many peripheral conformal papers (class-conditional, efficiency, time series, clinical applications). It does not cite the foundational and directly-used sources: the baseline score functions, split/Mondrian conformal, and weighted conformal under covariate shift. `references.bib` contains no Vovk, Romano, Angelopoulos, Tibshirani (weighted) or Aitchison entries. The appendix already acknowledges that these are \"stated as background without citation\".\n\n## Missing literatures\n- Split (inductive) and Mondrian conformal prediction foundations\n- Weighted conformal prediction under covariate shift\n- Conformal classification scores (LAC, APS, RAPS)\n- Compositional data analysis (Aitchison log-ratio geometry)\n\n## Targets\n\n1. **baseline-score-sources** (high, comparator) — Method, \"Baselines, negative controls and validity conditions\". The headline claim is a margin over the best of LAC/APS/RAPS/class-wise LAC, yet none of these is cited. Search: LAC / least-ambiguous set classifiers; APS; RAPS; class-wise split conformal.\n2. **mondrian-split-conformal-foundations** (high, background) — Method, \"Statistical background\". The Proposition and rank argument are called textbook but unsourced, and Mondrian calibration is the core of the method. Search: Mondrian conformal prediction (Vovk et al.); split/inductive conformal; distribution-free finite-sample coverage.\n3. **weighted-conformal-shift-and-compositional-framing** (medium, positioning) — Method, \"Weighted calibration under covariate shift\", and Related Work, \"Positioning\". The gated weighting step and the shift axis lack their source (weighted conformal under covariate shift; classifier-based density ratios). The log-ratio compositional framing is uncited. Search: conformal under covariate shift; probabilistic-classifier density-ratio estimation; Aitchison compositional data.\n\n## Deliberately ignored\n- Quantitative results (grounded in `paper_data.json`).\n- Further applied or tutorial conformal papers, and the existing Related Work paragraphs on other output types.\n- Real-data or CIFAR-10 literature, which would require reshaping the paper's synthetic-only scope.\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}}}
