ed cumulative-mass score) is one of the four baselines in the best-baseline margin claim and has no citation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"uncertainty sets for image classifiers using conformal prediction regularized adaptive prediction sets RAPS\",\n      \"category\": \"baseline_comparator\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Gap target baseline-score-sources: RAPS (APS with rank penalty) is a baseline in the headline comparison and is uncited; this query is paragraph-specific to the baseline description.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"Mondrian conformal prediction category-conditional validity inductive split conformal foundations\",\n      \"category\": \"core_method\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Gap target mondrian-split-conformal-foundations (Method, 'Statistical background'): the Proposition and rank argument are called textbook but unsourced, and Mondrian calibration is the core of the method; only recent conditional-validity papers are in the bibliography.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"conformal prediction under covariate shift weighted exchangeability likelihood ratio\",\n      \"category\": \"core_method\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Gap target weighted-conformal-shift-and-compositional-framing (Method, 'Weighted calibration under covariate shift'; Related Work, 'Positioning'): the gated weighting with test-point mass at +infinity rests on weighted conformal under covariate shift, which is uncited and has no Related Work paragraph despite shift being an evaluation axis. Classifier-based density-ratio weights are covered here by the same retrieval rather than a separate query.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"Aitchison statistical analysis of compositional data log-ratio geometry simplex\",\n      \"category\": \"benchmark_context\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Gap target weighted-conformal-shift-and-compositional-framing (Introduction and Related Work 'Positioning'): the draft frames softmax outputs as compositions and invokes log-ratio compositional